> 2. Is there an option that will improve the inventory interface or is the
> default all there is(trying to make the transition from ADOM)?

There are four "menustyles" available - the default, "full", will give
you a lot of menus of all items you can perform an action with, often
with "preliminary" menus in which you can first choose the actual type
of objects you wish to choose from. 
"traditional" is the most terse - it will often just give you prompts,
one item at a time, or displays the letters of eligible objects on the
message line; you can request a full menu in most cases, though. 
The "in-between" menustyles of "partial" and "combined" are, i think,
closest to the way Adom handles inventory - just flush the full
inventory and let you pick (except that a NetHack main inventory won't
stretch over twenty pages).
Enter "O"ptions, page down until "menustyles" appears and try them
out. 

If you want to do something with _part_ of a stack of identical items,
this can at times be achieved by preceding the inventory letter by a
number, e.g. "d2p"- drop two items from slot "p". "D" is a useful
"extended-drop" command, to leave behind/sell/get rid of multiple
items at the same time. If you want to drop only part of a stack here,
once again type the number of items you desire to leave before
entering the inventory letter.

The options "autoquiver" and "packorder" also allow some
customisation. 

And much more can be gleaned from the online help (just hit "?"
in-game) or from the guidebook (should have gotten it as part of the
documentation), like menu shortcuts, many more options etc.

